    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure - Original Motion Picture Soundtrack, released in 1989 by A&M Records, is a vibrant collection of rock tracks that perfectly captures the energetic and irreverent spirit of the cult classic film. Featuring a mix of hard rock, pop rock, and new wave, the album showcases performances by artists such as Extreme, Shark Island, Big Pig, and Glen Burtnick. The music ranges from high-octane guitar-driven anthems like \"Play With Me\" by Extreme to more melodic tracks like \"Not So Far Away\" by Glen Burtnick, reflecting the film's blend of comedy, adventure, and youthful exuberance.\n\nAs a soundtrack, the album stands as a notable entry in the discographies of the featured artists, particularly Extreme, whose inclusion helped boost their early exposure. The album's track order differs from the film, but it remains a snapshot of late-1980s rock, with several songs becoming fan favorites and enduring as part of the film's legacy. While not a major commercial blockbuster, the soundtrack was well-received for its energetic style and its ability to complement the film's tone, contributing to the overall success and lasting popularity of Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure.",
      "generated_at": "2025-11-27T13:54:33.132070",
